+**Changes requested.** The skill can discard a valid discovery proposal, misdescribe a refused miner run, and direct an agent toward the wrong field when reporting a learner’s claim. Several tests pass when the instructions they guard are reversed. All 53 SHA-256 digests matched the brief, and the live Git diff matched the supplied patch byte for byte.
+
+## Findings
+
+| ID | File and line | Finding and reproduction |
+|---|---|---|
+| F1 | [gnd-induce/SKILL.md:64](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L64) | **`EMITTED 0` can accompany a valid proposal.** I ran discovery in memory on 20 distinct items with one single-valued attribute each and `--families fact-type`. It printed `EMITTED 0` and `FACT TYPES 1`, and built a proposal with two operations. The instruction to “hand nothing off” loses that proposal. Use the report’s `proposal` field to decide the handoff. The judge route at line 69 also needs `--type-evidence` when judgements are requested. The documented invocation produces no evidence file for either judge. |
+| F2 | [gnd-induce/SKILL.md:120](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L120) | **AMIE import refuses the whole set on the first failing rule.** “GND keeps only the rules … that hold” suggests partial admission. Importing the shipped `staffing/learners/amie` rules and record returned exit 3 on rule 0, with 19 of 20 head pairs holding, and produced no proposal. An agent following the skill could report a retained subset that GND never wrote. |
+| F3 | [gnd-induce/SKILL.md:158](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L158) | **The handoff assigns `inducer` to the assembled run record.** The record has `learner`. GND writes `inducer` into the proposal’s induction provenance. I added `inducer` to the shipped Popper record in memory and validated it. The closed schema rejected the additional property. T8 at line 98 currently requires the misleading wording. |
+| F4 | [gnd-induce/SKILL.md:73](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L73) | **The learner instructions omit the class-mode prerequisite and the neutral fallback.** Running the labelled export with the shipped `ik5-corpus/es.labels.json` returned exit 3 because expected-state manifests have no class labels to learn from. At line 83, “offer the export alone” leaves the previously selected target in effect, although §6.1 specifies a neutral export when the named learner is missing. Ask the host for a class-mode manifest and name `--target neutral` in the fallback. |
+| F5 | [gnd-induce/SKILL.md:3](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L3), [line 50](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L50), [line 104](src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md#L104) | **Three claims disagree with executable examples.** The description calls every output a proposal. Scoring the refunds fixture returned a measurement report. It printed six cells for one rule, including `vacuous` and `unchecked`, whereas line 50 says one cell per rule and label. Line 104 says Popper has never run on GND’s examples. The bridge records three refunds runs, and I re-imported the shipped Popper program and record successfully with one admitted clause and support `4/4`. The summary also says four commands at line 10, and line 170 places every reference in `gnd-orm-core` despite the external ILP bridge link at line 84. |
+| F6 | [test_packaged_skills.py:247](tests/test_packaged_skills.py#L247), [test_induce_skill.py:108](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L108) | **The route tests accept reversed judge destinations.** I swapped the two link targets at skill line 69, leaving their visible labels intact. The matrix and D23 tests passed. Clicking “duplicates” would open the multi-valued judge. The matrix looks for the trigger, destination and boundary independently across a whole file. The judge test checks only that both URLs occur in the section. Bind each trigger to its actual link in the rendered sentence or table row. |
+| F7 | [test_induce_skill.py:55](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L55) | **T8 counts files containing a refusal, rather than occurrences visible to a reader.** Appending R-e a second time inside `gnd-induce/SKILL.md` still returned exactly `["gnd-induce/SKILL.md"]`. Wrapping R-c in an HTML comment also passed. The second-file control catches a different failure. Count visible occurrences and seed a duplicate in the original file as well. |
+| F8 | [test_induce_skill.py:85](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L85) | **T8 accepts instructions that reverse the authority boundary.** I replaced the LLM paragraph’s separate-agent-and-stop instruction with “Answer the prompt here and construct its run record.” The D21 test passed. The handoff test also passed with “Even if no command exited 0 and emitted something,” and the reactions test passed after deleting the exit-11 row. These are changes to the instructions themselves, within the spec’s stated scope for text tests. Pin the user-run evidence-script route, the positive handoff condition and the required table rows. |
+| F9 | [test_public_packaged_invocation_guards.py:132](tests/test_public_packaged_invocation_guards.py#L132), [test_public_packaged_command_help.py:31](tests/test_public_packaged_command_help.py#L31) | **The invocation checks miss both missing commands and invalid options.** I measured 41 snippets, but the global floor remains 29. Replacing the mined-rules import with a second `gnd check` kept the per-skill test green. Adding a valid tilde-fenced shell block left the discovered count at seven. Replacing `--families` with `--type` passed the help-option test because the substring occurs in help. The CLI rejected it as ambiguous with exit 64. Pin the required command paths and compare complete option names. |
+| F10 | [test_induce_skill.py:65](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L65), [line 175](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L175) | **The section and index matchers disagree with rendered Markdown.** Two trailing spaces on `## Learn` made T8 report a missing section. Moving the entire index row into a fenced text example passed T17, leaving readers with no table entry. Changing its final command to `gnd checker` also passed the `gnd check` substring test. Read the heading and table structure, then compare the command cells. |
+| F11 | [test_induce_skill.py:113](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L113), [line 153](tests/test_induce_skill.py#L153) | **The actor, installation and path guards miss ordinary inputs.** I changed every proposal command to `--actor operator`, appended an instruction to obtain the actor with `git var GIT_AUTHOR_IDENT`, and tried `pip3 install popper`. Each corresponding test passed. The absolute-path patterns also accepted `/srv/reviewer/runs/april`. These edits would publish a fixed or Git-derived actor, an installation instruction, or a host path while the named guards remained green. |
+| F12 | [regressions-red.txt:4](.gnd-planning/milestones/induction-skill/evidence/IS1/regressions-red.txt#L4), [line 58](.gnd-planning/milestones/induction-skill/evidence/IS1/regressions-red.txt#L58) | **The required T16 red and T17 commit ordering are missing.** Control 1 omits `test_public_built_inventory.py`. Its 17 passing cases are recorded only on the completed tree. Control 2 does record T17 failing with the row withheld. Git history, however, first adds T17 and its documentation row together in `9090e84a`. That demonstrates a withheld-row failure but does not satisfy §5’s “committed before its row” requirement. |
+
+## What passed
+
+I independently ran **405 read-only test cases**. The current tree has 19 skills, 73 packaged files, all 15 new route edges and 265 relative-link occurrences. Both discovery links are tracked at symlink mode `120000`. The vendored label schema matches the runtime bytes. The base has 18 skills and 71 files, missing exactly the two newly pinned paths.
+
